,"/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same pair came in at 57% of normal, and November to December at 47%. So far in 2026, January to February sits at 46% and February to March at 48% on the middle of the grids. Grid 15147 had its driest year in 1954 at 58% of normal.</p>"}
